<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        U3 / S7 — the Owl export preview and diff surface.

        A client action rather than a form view, because what a reviewer needs
        to read here is not a record's fields: it is a *difference*, with a
        removal section, a refusal section and an untouched section that each
        carry their own severity. A `widget="json"` dump of the diff field
        shows the same bytes and communicates none of that.

        It reads exactly one read-only aggregate
        (`shopify.connector.product.export.ui.get_export_preview_data`) and its
        only write path is `action_confirm_export_preview` — the same
        sanctioned server door the wizard uses, with the same server-side role,
        state, expiry and plan checks. The screen is a face; the backend is the
        authority.
    -->

    <!--
        NO `group_ids` HERE, AND THAT IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT. `group_ids` exists
        on `ir.actions.act_window` and `ir.actions.server` but NOT on
        `ir.actions.client` (odoo/odoo@19.0 `ir_actions.py::IrActionsClient`,
        verified against the pinned source) — declaring one is a hard
        ParseError at install, not a silently ignored field.

        Access is therefore enforced where it actually belongs and where a
        client action cannot route around it:

        * the Export menu branch and the button that opens this action both
          carry `groups="…group_shopify_connector_user"`, which is VISIBILITY;
        * `get_export_preview_data` raises `AccessError` for any caller
          outside the connector groups, and reads the preview as the current
          user so the ordinary ACL and the SEC-3 company record rules apply;
        * `action_confirm_export_preview` re-checks Administrator authority
          under a row lock, which is AUTHORIZATION.

        A user who reached this tag by hand gets an AccessError from the
        service, not a rendered screen.
    -->
    <record id="action_shopify_connector_export_diff" model="ir.actions.client">
        <field name="name">Review Export</field>
        <field name="tag">shopify_connector_export_diff</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
